Notes on grading: both were called 4 ("well-defined radiolucent areas") rather than 3 (diffuse mineral-loss changes only) because each shows a circumscribed dark zone centered on the apex; neither shows the aggressive, ill-defined expansile pattern of PAI 5. The lower arch and remaining upper teeth showed no convincing periapical rarefaction at this resolution — the repeated dark wedges between posterior crowns are interproximal/occlusal overlap shadows, not periapical lesions (though several crowns do contain what look like carious defects, which are outside the scope of periapical scoring).

I've completed a systematic review of the radiograph — full-view, quadrant zooms, background-subtraction to highlight diffuse radiolucencies, a focal-darkness component scan, and gray-value comparison of each apex zone against neighboring teeth. Here is my assessment:

**Findings:**

1. **Mandibular right first molar (image left, ~x 0.30–0.37)** — root-canal treated with a full-coverage crown. There is a well-demarcated radiolucency involving the furcation region and extending around both mesial and distal root apices, with loss of the normal trabecular pattern compared to the adjacent premolar/molar apex zones. The endodontic filling also terminates short of the radiographic apices. This is a **well-defined radiolucent area → PAI 4**.

2. **Mandibular left first molar (image right, ~x 0.62–0.70)** — also root-canal treated with a crown. Periapical bone shows diffusely increased radiolucency with altered, coarsened trabeculation around the mesial root apex and furcal area, but without a sharply corticated lucency. This fits **changes in bone structure with some mineral loss → PAI 3**.

**Excluded as normal anatomy:** the maxillary anterior apex darkening (nasal fossa/incisive foramen superimposition), the upper molar apex zones (sinus floor proximity), the dark wedge between the upper right premolars (projection artifact of tipped teeth/open embrasure), the mandibular canal, and the mental foramen region. No lesions found in the remaining quadrants.

